{#-
  The AFUI-owned remote page. It may list the machine's registered sessions or
  carry exactly one session for a direct link.

  Every id comes from `document.elements` and every card class from
  `document.card`, so a replacement page cannot misspell one and a page that
  drops one is reported before the listener binds. Actions and sizes are
  declared rather than wired: the runtime reads `data-act` and `data-size` and
  decides what pressing one does, so a control can be relabelled, reordered or
  dropped without it becoming a control that does something else.

  The script is not here. AFUI splices its own runtime in at the marker below,
  and a frontend may not supply JavaScript at all.
-#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ document.lang }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>{{ document.title }}</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="__afui/app-icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="__afui/base.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="shell.css">
  <!-- afui:trusted-runtime -->
</head>
<body data-ui-api-version="{{ document.ui_api_version }}">
  <header class="bar">
    <h1>{{ document.heading }}</h1>
    <p id="{{ document.elements.state_line }}" class="state">
      <span id="{{ document.elements.count }}">0</span> {{ document.words.open_count }} ·
      <span id="{{ document.elements.state }}">{{ document.words.connecting }}</span>
    </p>
  </header>

  <p id="{{ document.elements.notice }}" class="notice" role="status" hidden>
    <span id="{{ document.elements.notice_text }}"></span>
    <button type="button" id="{{ document.elements.notice_renew }}">{{ document.renew_label }}</button>
  </p>

  <main class="deck">
    <section class="pane list-pane" aria-label="{{ document.heading }}">
      <div class="pane-head"><h2>{{ document.slot_heading }}</h2></div>
      <div id="{{ document.elements.slot }}" class="stack"></div>
      <p id="{{ document.elements.empty }}" class="empty">{{ document.empty_label }}</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <template id="{{ document.elements.card }}">
    <article class="{{ document.card.root }}">
      {#- The head of a card is a bar with three parts, in the order every
          window a person has used puts them: one slot for getting out of where
          you are, then what you are looking at, then what can be done to the
          card holding it.

          A control drawn as a glyph carries its label as its name rather than
          as its face — the glyph itself is `aria-hidden`, so what is announced
          and what a pointer rests on is the word, not the picture. A
          replacement that prefers words drops the glyph and prints
          `action.label`; nothing here reads the face back. -#}
      <header class="card-head">
        {%- for action in document.actions %}{% if action.slot == 'navigation' %}
        <button type="button" class="act-icon act-nav" {{ document.action_attribute }}="{{ action.name }}" aria-label="{{ action.label }}" title="{{ action.label }}"{% if action.hidden %} hidden{% endif %}><span aria-hidden="true">{{ action.glyph }}</span></button>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
        <div class="who">
          <strong class="{{ document.card.provider }}"></strong>
          <span class="{{ document.card.kind }}"></span>
          <span class="{{ document.card.subject }}"></span>
        </div>
        {#- What the interface inside the frame says about itself, which is the
            one part of this bar the frame cannot know. It sits between the
            title and the controls, the way a window's own status always has. -#}
        <span class="{{ document.card.page_status }}" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
        <div class="acts">
          <span class="{{ document.card.action_status }}" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
          {#- The link is a link, so a long press offers the browser's own menu. -#}
          <a class="{{ document.card.open }} act-icon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="{{ document.open_label }}" title="{{ document.open_label }}" hidden><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          {%- for action in document.actions %}{% if action.slot == 'action' %}
          {%- if action.glyph %}
          <button type="button" class="act-icon" {{ document.action_attribute }}="{{ action.name }}" aria-label="{{ action.label }}" title="{{ action.label }}"{% if action.hidden %} hidden{% endif %}><span aria-hidden="true">{{ action.glyph }}</span></button>
          {%- else %}
          <button type="button" {{ document.action_attribute }}="{{ action.name }}"{% if action.hidden %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ action.label }}</button>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
          <details class="act-menu">
            <summary class="act-icon" role="button" aria-label="{{ document.more_label }}" title="{{ document.more_label }}"><span aria-hidden="true">⋮</span></summary>
            <div class="act-menu-items">
              {%- for action in document.actions %}{% if action.slot == 'menu' %}
              <button type="button" {{ document.action_attribute }}="{{ action.name }}"{% if action.hidden %} hidden{% endif %}>{{ action.label }}</button>
              {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </header>
      <p class="{{ document.card.notice }}" role="status" hidden></p>
      <div class="{{ document.card.frame }}"></div>
    </article>
  </template>
</body>
</html>
